<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis XV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1710–1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis XV was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1715 to 1774, succeeding his great-grandfather <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> at the age of five. His reign saw French defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> and the loss of most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>. The crown also bought out the last semi-independent lordships inside the kingdom, such as the Principality of Dombes and the Viscounty of Turenne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-xv.jpg" alt="Louis XV" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Louis-Michel van Loo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_XV,_King_of_France_(1710-1774)_edited_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
